But what does it mean, oral law?

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:07.200
In other words, what does it mean, written law

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:07.680
or oral law?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:12.060
The proper translation of Torah,

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.100
Shebe Adbe,

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:16.720
in Spanish,

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.040
I use this for English also,

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.640
Le Mental.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:23.380
The Le, the law,

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.740
as is grasped in your mind.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.300
Because, yes, you have a text,

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:35.220
but there's always a distance

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.780
between what is written

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:41.140
and what is captured in your mind.

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:43.560
That may as well subject it.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:44.700
Absolutely.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.660
That's what we say in the morning.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.020
Shema Yisrael.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:51.920
We say Shema, humankind.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.420
It is for us.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.560
We do not want to convert anybody.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.660
We don't want to convince anybody.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.800
Yes, our art,

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:02.680
our skills and rhetoric

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.360
is not to convince other people

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:07.060
to become Jews.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:08.580
but to sell our merchandise.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.920
That's all.

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:14.080
Torah is

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:17.300
Shema

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.220
Israel.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:22.180
It's subjective. That is the way

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.300
we understand. And precisely

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.480
here is the difference.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.120
Because we understand that

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.140
this is subjective.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.940
This is Am Yisrael.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.100
We do not

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.080
want to convert

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.220
anybody.

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:45.060
Yes? And we say, Noah, Hasidim of the people of the world, yes I am the prophet of God.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:50.060
I think I told you last year, the story which is a fantastic story, the book is translated into English,

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:54.060
it's worth reading, Rabbeleahu Ben Hamosek.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:18:00.060
The priest and so on, wants to become Jewish, and so on,

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:10.860
he comes to Rabbi Adam Ben Amozek and he says, I want to be Jewish. He says, why? He's a priest.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:20.500
Olam Abba! He says, Olam Abba, fulfill the challenge of the Lord. And it was a beautiful

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:28.180
dialogue. It is translated in English. It's called The Unknown Sanctuary by Peyer. Peyer

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:32.380
was the author, the priest, and the Zivetes, we don't want you to convert anybody.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.180
You are Arab, you are going, you are Arab.

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:40.100
Show me something I know. You have to be Jewish. And he said to him, you know what?

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:44.220
Yes, you are fantastic. Only a Jew has this kind of wife. He said to him,

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:46.040
you have parents? Yes.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:51.460
And are they happy that you want to convert into Jewish?

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:56.140
He says, no. You want to convert to Judaism

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:57.900
