the law of operates in Judaism in Judaism we have two laws I mean I'm

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:49.780
Also, the Torah, the written Torah.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:55.300
And we have the oral, what is called oral Torah.

00:19:56.600 --> 00:20:03.040
Law, which is enforceable by the courts, is only Torah.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:07.540
In other words, suppose you bring a pasuk from the Torah,

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:12.320
and you do not document it through Torah, it's not binding.

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:24.060
That's why it says, what is binding, what you see, the word muswa, from the word of savlui, yes, which is enforced by the court, is to be described there.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:25.660
Alright, that is the law.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:32.080
Alright, now, therefore, this is part of the collective mind of Israel.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:33.680
I can't come to, I've explained everything.

